247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (The UFC stands as the undisputed global leader in Mixed Martial Arts, renowned for its high-energy entertainment and elite competition. This has fostered a loyal and diverse fanbase, solidifying its position as a dominant brand. Simultaneously, the MMA market is experiencing rapid growth, driven by mainstream acceptance, strong digital and social media presence, and successful international expansion. However, the UFC faces critical challenges, including managing the perception of violence, handling fighter controversies, and adapting to evolving audience expectations, with a particular emphasis on prioritizing athlete health, both mental and physical.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 196 0 R
/E (Despite these challenges, the UFC has significant strategic opportunities. It can leverage its brand power as a platform for positive social impact, expanding its reach to new demographics and strengthening its brand through responsible advocacy. Notably, the UFC has the opportunity to become a leader in athlete mental health, promoting the well-being of its athletes.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
